plan rule 'each candidate group no larger than its base group': FAIL (accepted by Joe, 2026-10-04: matplotlib's simplifier sits between a line's data and its bytes)
D2, every other rule and the per-file finding: PASS

The plan's rule "each candidate group is no larger than its base group" FAILED on R9's altitude envelope (the SVG, and
the same figure in the batch report): 25 of 58 groups are larger, by 1 to 47 bytes (164 in total); 22 of them at an
equal drawn vertex count (coordinate digit length), 3 with 1 or 2 more drawn vertices. Cause: matplotlib's path
simplifier sits between a line's data and its bytes. It already draws each smooth 10,000-point altitude overlay as
about 40 vertices, at base and after, and the reduction only moves where those vertices fall, so fewer data points
do not give fewer drawn vertices or bytes per line. Joe (2026-10-04) accepted it as a recorded failure with no code
change; the plan is not edited. The per-file finding in its place (above): the overlay groups' total bytes and drawn
vertex count are no larger in all three files, and every byte outside them is identical.
T6's bound on the altitude overlays: at most 43 drawn vertices in one group (above), and at most 905 data points in
one overlay (D4's "most points", below), each within 3 x 900 + 1 = 2,701.

